+---
+id: task-001-spring-newsletter-discount-codes
+type: task
+title: "Spring newsletter discount codes"
+status: approved
+format: 1
+---
+
+# Spring newsletter discount codes
+
+Customers get discount codes in the newsletter for the spring campaign. An order takes one code at most.
+
+## What the request asks
+
+- `SPRING10`: 10 % off the order's items, rounded to the nearest cent (a half cent rounds up).
+- `WELCOME5`: 5.00 € off the order's items, only on an order whose items come to 30.00 € or more.
+- A second code replaces the first. An unknown code, or `WELCOME5` on a smaller order, is refused with an
+  error that says why, and the order is left as it was.
+- The discount never touches shipping. Whether an order ships free is decided on its items before any discount.
+- The order book offers `applyCode(orderNumber, code)`. An order's totals show `discountCents` (0 without a code)
+  and `totalCents` as items minus discount plus shipping.
+
+## Acceptance
+
+- `applyCode` applies a code to an order and returns its totals; an unknown order, an unknown code, or a code whose
+  condition the order does not meet is refused with the reason, and the order keeps its previous code (if any).
+- `totals` reports `itemsCents`, `discountCents`, `shippingCents` and `totalCents = items - discount + shipping`.
+- Tests cover both codes, the rounding of `SPRING10`, the `WELCOME5` threshold, replacement of a code, refusal, and
+  shipping being decided before the discount.
+
+## Decisions taken while building
+
+- Codes are matched without regard to case and surrounding spaces.
+- `applyCode` returns the order's totals, so the caller sees the discount at once.
